.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-ABORT-UPLOAD 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-abort-upload \- throw away a multipart upload that will not be finished
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm abort-upload
.BR \-\-upload\-id | \-u
.I ID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discards a multipart upload: the parts staged on disk under
.IR ID ,
and \- for a first upload \- the object row
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1)
seeded for bytes that never arrived.
.PP
This is the counterpart
.I complete-upload
has always needed. An upload that stops halfway leaves scratch storage under
an id nothing will ever complete, and nothing else can tell the difference
between an upload that was abandoned and one that is still being sent.
.SH WHAT SURVIVES
A
.I re-upload
\- an upload to a key that already holds an object \- leaves that object
exactly as it is. The row is the previous version: still published, still
readable, and not this upload's to delete. Only a first upload's row is
removed, because it describes an object whose bytes never arrived.
.PP
The answer says which happened in
.IR objectRemoved .
The distinction matters: "the upload is gone" and "the object is gone" are
different outcomes, and a caller cleaning up after a failure needs to know
which one they got.
.SH WHEN YOU NEED IT
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1)
does not need this \- it completes or it fails within one command. What needs
it is an upload nothing is driving any more:
.TP
.B a client that went away
A machine rebooted, a process killed, a network that dropped mid-upload.
.TP
.B a gateway upload that was refused
An upload route abandons its upload when a part is refused, when
.I complete-upload
fails, or when the body does not match the
.I Content-Digest
that was signed. It calls this action itself; the id is in its log if the
call did not get through.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload\-id " " \fIID\fR
The upload to discard, as
.I create-upload
returned it. Required.
.SH OUTPUT
The upload's id, the bucket and key it was being written to, how many staged
parts were thrown away, and whether the object row went with it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The upload was discarded.
.TP
.B 1
Missing arguments, the server could not be reached, the caller's grants do
not cover the bucket, or there is no such upload. An upload that has already
completed answers \fIHTTP 404\fR, because there is no longer any such upload.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli esm abort-upload \e
    --upload-id 3f2a9c14-7b60-4c1e-9a0d-2f5e8b7c1d04
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-create-route (1)
